> > The skill now takes a notmuch id. Without one it still falls back to
> > the oldest inbox message, so /process-email by hand works as before.
> > A message that is no longer in the inbox ends the pass without
> > writing, because someone has already answered or archived it.
> 
> Simplify this so an argument is required.

Done in v3. /process-email now requires the id and answers only that
message; with no argument it stops without writing. It no longer runs
`just get-oldest-inbox-message` itself, so that recipe moved into "just:
Add just process-email", the loop being its only caller. The separate
"Find the oldest message with just" patch is gone.

> We are moving logic out of inference and into determinism. So wherever
> we can do that, we should.

Agreed. Choosing the message was the last part of picking work that
the model still did. Now the loop chooses, and the skill only does
what needs judgement.

The revised series is "[PATCH v3 0/6] Add just process-email" [1]. It
also drops the skill's loop mode and adds the "E: " prefix, as asked
in "Re: [PATCH v2 3/7] just: Add just process-email" [2].

Thanks for the review.

